# Bug bounty Part 1: Information Gathering
Platform: Bugcrowd
Target: web application (program name not shared)
Scope: in-scope assets only, program rules followed

## What I did (passive OSINT)
- Google dorks to find indexed pages and publik files of the target
- Wayback Machine to check old versions of pages and old endpoints
- BuiltWith to identify the technologies used (CMS, framework, analytics)
- Netcraft to check hosting information and site history

## Today, I worked with these four tools using the assistance of Gemini AI.
- I asked the AI for commands on how to operate-using placeholders like "example.com" to avoid revealing the actual company name-and then manually entered and tested those commands myself.
- At the beginning and end of the session, I performed full system scans using ESET, Malwarebytes, Bitdefender Antivirus, and Windows Defender.
- Finally, I completely cleared my brouser and terminal history, deleted any company-related files from the computer, and shut the machine down. 
- Today, I used my real IP address on the computer where I accessed Gemini AI, while using a VPN on the computer I use for bug bounty work.
